{\plain We can use a "trick"! Recall that
 a triangle waveshape is the result of convolving
 a\par rectangular wave shape with itself.
 And, in the FT domain this is a multiplication
 of the\par waveforms's FT with itself. 
After working out the details we find}
}
.EQN 13 5 46 0
{0:V}NAME:1
.EQN 0 13 37 0
{0:F}NAME({0:\w}NAME):{0:\t}NAME*{0:V}NAME*((({0:sin}NAME(({0:\w}NAME*{0:\t}NAME)/(2)))/(({0:\w}NAME*{0:\t}NAME)/(2))))^(2)
